    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ae72852ec358ff536a3381f8102283f71b843a88a2f33f12c023d9415ae9efbf",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-337d155f29274612b31edc8084c70ab0",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Early transfer to the pier.\n\nThe full-day trip begins with a ride in motorised curiaras up the Carrao River to Mayupa Lagoon and the Arautaima current.\n\nAfter a short crossing, arrive at a camp overlooking the Auyán-tepui massif.\n\nLight breakfast.\n\nContinue towards Devil’s Canyon. On reaching Ratón Island, set out on foot through the forest.\n\nAfter about an hour, the group reaches a viewpoint facing Angel Falls.\n\nThe water drops almost 1 km here.\n\nIf you wish to swim, local guides may offer the chance to do so in the lagoon at the foot of the falls.\n\nAfter visiting the falls, return to Canaima Lagoon.\n\nA traditional Indigenous lunch is included.\n\nDinner and overnight at the hotel.\n\n**Important:** This day is designed for active travellers. The programme runs from approximately 05:00 to 18:00 and includes motorboat rides, walking and a short trek through the jungle.\n\nBring trainers or hiking shoes, comfortable clothes and a change of clothes. A raincoat is recommended in the rainy season.\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast, lunch and dinner."
    },
